{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00473",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.98,
      "end_seconds": 8.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Yeah, hi doctor, sorry, the lift was out and I had to take the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.37,
      "end_seconds": 13.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.61,
      "end_seconds": 23.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor. We came because of alternating constipation and loose stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.04,
      "end_seconds": 26.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.49,
      "end_seconds": 30.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "For nearly five years, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.89,
      "end_seconds": 34.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "How would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.55,
      "end_seconds": 36.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.82,
      "end_seconds": 43.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Alright, anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.75,
      "end_seconds": 77.49,
      "duration_seconds": 33.74,
      "text": "Cramping pain in the lower tummy goes along with it, most of the time. As for cramping pain in the lower tummy, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. As for cramping pain in the lower tummy, about a six out of ten. It's once or twice a day. I've also been passing a lot of wind, for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.32,
      "end_seconds": 82.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "With passing a lot of wind, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.98,
      "end_seconds": 86.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.3,
      "end_seconds": 105.47,
      "duration_seconds": 17.17,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest. No, I don't smoke and never have. I eat out quite a lot, to be honest. I share a flat with two friends."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.19,
      "end_seconds": 110.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Tell me about your health in general, any ongoing conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.06,
      "end_seconds": 125.88,
      "duration_seconds": 13.82,
      "text": "Yes, anxiety. I've had acid reflux, yes. I just want to get back to normal, really. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.45,
      "end_seconds": 133.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.06,
      "text": "Alright, acid reflux, that matches what I have here. What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.83,
      "end_seconds": 141.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "I'm on omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 141.91,
      "end_seconds": 148.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "She is supposed to take it once a day, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.89,
      "end_seconds": 153.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I take Colospa, when it cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.3,
      "end_seconds": 168.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Alright, any procedures or operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.95,
      "end_seconds": 181.05,
      "duration_seconds": 11.1,
      "text": "I, I had my appendix out about eight years ago. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.28,
      "end_seconds": 190.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "How about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.0,
      "end_seconds": 193.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Definitely no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 195.48,
      "end_seconds": 200.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.0,
      "end_seconds": 213.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "No, um, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.4,
      "end_seconds": 223.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any weight loss or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.1,
      "end_seconds": 229.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "No. None of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.33,
      "end_seconds": 233.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.51,
      "end_seconds": 235.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.52,
      "end_seconds": 241.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Let's get your blood pressure and the other basics."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.32,
      "end_seconds": 249.17,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "One second..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.22,
      "end_seconds": 274.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.7, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, pressure 108 over 74, pulse 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.28,
      "end_seconds": 280.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Okay, I need to examine you for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.45,
      "end_seconds": 286.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.24,
      "end_seconds": 302.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Soft tummy, a bit tender on the left lower side, no masses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.58,
      "end_seconds": 327.95,
      "duration_seconds": 19.37,
      "text": "Thanks, please take a seat again. From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Coeliac disease is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.76,
      "end_seconds": 332.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Is this something I'll have for good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.82,
      "end_seconds": 341.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.91,
      "end_seconds": 370.4,
      "duration_seconds": 16.49,
      "text": "Blood tests is what I'd like next, for bowel symptoms. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. A coeliac test is what I'd like next, for bloating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.03,
      "end_seconds": 373.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.46,
      "end_seconds": 388.13,
      "duration_seconds": 13.67,
      "text": "Regular meals and a bit more fibre, and don't rush your toilet time. Come back after the results are back. Okay, good. Let us know how you get on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.84,
      "end_seconds": 393.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "That's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.57,
      "end_seconds": 397.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Mind how you go."
    }
  ]
}